---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Work With Me" description="Martin Swinkels is a freelance DevOps engineer for deployment platforms, golden paths and Azure governance, working remotely from Portugal.">
  <div class="hero single">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Freelance &middot; 1 to 3 days a week &middot; Remote from Portugal</div>
      <h1>Bring structure to <em>how your teams deploy</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Working alongside your developers and engineers, I set up the platforms and golden paths that make deploying to Azure the same every time, then hand them over or keep improving them with your team.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>What I Help With</h2>
      <div class="work-grid">
        <article><h3>Azure Platform</h3><p>A solid base on Azure: landing zones, governance, access control, naming and policy, set up as code and rolled out through pipelines.</p><div class="chips"><span>Bicep</span><span>Terraform</span><span>Azure DevOps</span><span>Policy</span><span>Governance</span></div></article>
        <article><h3>Automation</h3><p>Scripts and small tools that check your environment, report on it and fix what drifts, so nobody has to do it by hand.</p><div class="chips"><span>PowerShell</span><span>REST</span><span>Pester</span><span>Script Analyzer</span></div></article>
        <article><h3>Deploy Platforms</h3><p>Golden paths, templates and guardrails that give teams a ready-made, safe way to deploy to Azure, with no passwords to manage.</p><div class="chips"><span>Golden Paths</span><span>GitHub</span><span>Platform Engineering</span></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>How We Work</h2>
      <ul class="now">
        <li><span class="tag">2 to 4 weeks</span><div><h3>A Quick Start</h3><p>One golden path, one pipeline or a landing zone baseline, working and documented.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="tag">Up to 3 months</span><div><h3>A Defined Result</h3><p>A landing zone, a complete deployment pipeline and a set of golden paths, delivered with code, documentation and a handover.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="tag">Up to 2 years</span><div><h3>Part of Your Team</h3><p>A steady platform or DevOps engineer for one to three days a week, working in your backlog and your repositories.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="tag">As needed</span><div><h3>Review and Advice</h3><p>A second opinion on a design, a pipeline or your way of deploying, before you commit to it.</p></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>Practical</h2>
      <ul class="now">
        <li><span class="tag">Availability</span><div><p>One to three days a week.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="tag">Location</span><div><p>Remote from the Algarve, Portugal, one hour behind the Netherlands. On site by arrangement.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="tag">Languages</span><div><p>Dutch, English and German.</p></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>Worked Example</h2>
      <div class="kite">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">MSCKite</div>
          <h3>Azure Platform Kite</h3>
          <p>Azure Platform Kite is my own toolkit for governed Azure delivery. It is being rolled out at a start-up and its customers, which shows what works in practice.</p>
          <p style="margin:0"><a class="more" href="https://github.com/msckite/az-platform-kite" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/msckite/az-platform-kite &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
        <img class="mark" src="/msckite-logo.png" width="800" height="540" alt="MSCKite logo" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <div class="contact">
        <p>Tell me what your teams are building and where deploying gets in the way.</p>
        <p class="meta" style="font-size:15px">You can reach me on LinkedIn, Bluesky or GitHub through the links in the footer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
